-- name    : ThreeSum.LightThreeSumHybrid.solves
-- status  : Proved
-- author  : @wurtle
-- created : 2026-10-14T19:23:14.373598+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/4f63dce9-d28a-4021-a1c8-d6d0b0e30d8d
-- title:
--   The complete hybrid program solves the formal original 3SUM task
-- statement:
--   For every natural $\kappa$, let $P_\kappa$ be the complete hybrid program, $T_\kappa(n,U)$ its certified hybrid time, and $R_\kappa(n,U)$ its resource need. Then
--   $$
--   \operatorname{Solves}(\mathrm{3SUM},P_\kappa,542,T_\kappa,R_\kappa).
--   $$
--   Explicitly, in every program $P_\kappa$ followed by any additional procedures, a valid task instance consists of a positive-length integer array stored below its free pointer with declared magnitude bound $U$. Whenever the limits accommodate $R_\kappa$ at that pointer and call depth, procedure $542$ terminates within $T_\kappa$ steps. It returns the Boolean indicator of a zero-sum triple at pairwise distinct original positions and preserves all memory below the free pointer.
--
--   This packages the concrete execution theorem into the benchmark's task interface, with the guarantee stable under appending procedures.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightThreeSumHybrid.lean#L69-L87

